The $\mathrm{SiW}_{12}$ of polyoxometalates, as reactive center, is supported in different cavities of MIL-101(Cr) by controlling the different synthesis methods, which enhanced the efficiency of photoexcited electron-hole pair separation.The synergistic effect of the porous MIL-101 $(\mathrm{Cr})$ and $\mathrm{SiW}_{12}$ greatly improves the nitrogen fixation efficiency of the composites.
